{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The fee is chargeable only if all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold, and limb (c) requires a continuous dwell of at least the 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the arrival marker. On the driver's own clean trace the longest continuous in-geofence run is 170 seconds (19:00:00 to 19:02:50), 130 seconds short of that minimum. The primary clause therefore does not make this wait sufficient, and the charge can stand only if the separate in-geofence intervals are added together at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-TRIP-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's complaint is exactly what the trace records: the driver was outside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 19:02:50 to 19:03:50, a 60-second absence during which he reached 179.8 m from the pin, and his own message at 19:02:30 announced that he had to circulate and would return to the same bay. A 170-second hold and a 160-second hold are not one continuous hold; the charge survives only if POL-NS-06(i) lets them be summed, and even then the accumulated 330 seconds clears the 300-second minimum by just 30 seconds (derived shortfall -30 s).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-CHAT-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.excursions",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record's wait_time_min of 6.2 minutes is not the measure POL-NS-01 limb (c) prescribes. It runs from the arrival marker and includes the 60 seconds during which the vehicle was away from the bay circulating, whereas the clause measures in-geofence dwell from the first qualifying fix. An elapsed six-minute figure taken from the trip record cannot supply the continuity that limb (c) requires and that the trace's 170-second longest run does not show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09107", "EV-GPS-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own position and the rider's silence are not part of this arithmetic. POL-NS-06 directs the refund to be decided on the dwell computation 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages', so the rider's track and the absence of any rider message during the waiting window cannot be used to convert a short in-geofence hold into a chargeable fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-CHAT-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-07 makes driver compensation payable only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. Because the continuous-dwell limb is not made out on the primary clause and the whole dispute is about whether the two holds may be added, the precondition for the SGD 3.20 compensation figure itemised in the fare breakdown is absent and no driver payment should issue.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09107", "EV-FARE-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The whole of the contested amount sits on the rider: the fare breakdown shows a single SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, with no booking or platform fee component to apportion. If the dwell requirement is not satisfied the cancellation-fee line falls away in full under POL-NS-06 and the return to the rider is the entire SGD 4.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09107", "EV-TRIP-09107"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.20,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.20,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 no-show fee charged to the rider stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.20 (80% of that fee). The case turns on whether the two stretches the car spent at the bay may be added together, and on this record they may.\n\nWhy the fee stands. POL-NS-01 requires four things, and all four hold. (a) The trip record records the driver's arrival at 19:00:20. (b) The GPS trace places him inside the 120 m arrival radius for this LARGE_VENUE pickup from 19:00:00, before that arrival marker; his closest fix was about 26 m from the pin and 35 of his 40 fixes qualify. (d) He terminated the trip at 19:06:30 under RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event, after the required dwell had accrued.\n\nThe disputed limb (c) – the 300-second dwell. The rider is right about the raw trace: the driver held for 170 seconds (19:00:00–19:02:50), left for 60 seconds, and held again for 160 seconds (19:03:50–19:06:30), so the longest single continuous hold is 170 seconds, 130 seconds short of 300. But POL-NS-06(i) expressly permits separate in-geofence intervals within one pickup attempt to be summed where the driver never travelled more than 300 m from the pin and a qualifying traffic advisory made holding position unlawfully impossible. Both conditions are met. His furthest point while circulating was 179.8 m from the pin, inside the 300 m leash, and LTA advisory ADV-20260907-01 is a CLOSURE covering the pickup road with an active window of 18:50 to 19:30, which covers the whole waiting period. The effective dwell is therefore 330 seconds, clearing the 300-second minimum by 30 seconds. His in-app messages at 19:02:30 ('kerb temporarily closed; I must circulate and will return to the same bay') and 19:04:05 ('Back at the marked bay now') describe exactly that lawful circulation, not an abandonment of the pickup.\n\nThe rider's point that trip_record.wait_time_min of 6.2 minutes is not the clause's yardstick is accepted: limb (c) measures in-geofence dwell from the first qualifying fix, not elapsed time from the arrival tap. It changes nothing here, because the properly measured dwell still meets the minimum. The rider's own absence from the pin (her fixes sit about 519 m away, outside the 150 m rider radius) and her silence in the chat likewise do not move the fee: POL-NS-06 decides the refund on the dwell arithmetic whether or not the rider was present or responsive. POL-NS-04 cannot apply because no rider locating message was sent, and POL-NS-05 does not apply because the arrival marker was placed while the driver sat inside the radius and stationary, not beyond 300 m or in motion.\n\nDriver compensation. With POL-NS-01 satisfied and nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80% of SGD 4.00, being SGD 3.20. The anti-farming check does not trip: 1 no-show termination in 30 days is below 4, and 1 divided by 120 completed trips is 0.008, below 0.08. Compensation is therefore payable rather than withheld, and the rider's charge stands.\n\nConfidence. Every artifact the ruling rests on – the GPS trace, trip record, chat log, fare breakdown and traffic advisory – carries weight 1.0 with no integrity defect under POL-NS-08 (no clock skew, no trace gap, the chat matches the trip record's message count, and the SGD 4.00 fee equals the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee), so nothing is discounted. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is engaged, and no clause directs a referral."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION","amount_sgd":3.20,"driver_compensation_sgd":3.20,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.92,"explanation":"Rider — your dispute is that the car left the bay, so the two separate waits should not be added together. On this record they may be added, and that is what decides the case. POL-NS-06(i) allows separate in-geofence intervals within a single pickup attempt to be summed where two conditions hold, and both hold here. First, the driver never travelled more than 300 m from the pin: his furthest point during the 60-second circulation was 179.8 m (trace 19:02:50–19:03:50). Second, a qualifying traffic advisory was in force and populated — LTA advisory AD-20260907-107, type CLOSURE, weight 1.0, active 18:50–19:30 and covering the Orchard Central marked ride-hail bay, so its window covers the whole waiting period. With summation available, the effective in-geofence dwell is 330 seconds (170 s + 160 s) against the 300-second minimum for a LARGE_VENUE pickup, so POL-NS-01 limb (c) is met and POL-NS-06 requires no refund. Your remaining points are right in law but do not change the arithmetic: the trip record's 6.2-minute wait_time_min is not the measure the clause prescribes (the measure is accumulated in-geofence dwell, and it clears the minimum), and your own position and your silence are indeed irrelevant to the dwell computation under POL-NS-06 — I have not used them against you. The single in-geofence run of 170 s, and the 60-second absence, are real but they are precisely what the accumulation rule addresses.

Driver — your account is accepted. POL-NS-01 limb (a) is satisfied by the recorded arrival event at 19:00:20; limb (b) is satisfied because your first qualifying fix at 19:00:00 places you inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE radius at or before that event (35 of 40 fixes qualify); limb (c) is satisfied on the accumulated 330 seconds as above; and limb (d) is satisfied because the trip was terminated by you at 19:06:30 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee: POL-NS-03 does not apply because your stationary hold was inside the arrival radius, not outside it; POL-NS-04 does not apply because the rider sent no locating message during the waiting window; and POL-NS-05 does not apply because at 19:00:20 you were inside the radius and stationary, so there was no false marker and no recomputation of the clock. The SGD 4.00 fee reconciles with the fee schedule — the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) is SGD 4.00 — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect. POL-NS-07 therefore pays you 80 percent of the fee, SGD 3.20, and the anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination in 30 days, below 4, and 1/120 = 0.008, below 0.08). Per POL-NS-07 the disposition of the fee is that it stands; the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION because that is the outcome the case produces, and amount_sgd mirrors the driver payment.

Both parties — no artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08: clock skew is 20 seconds, the trace has no gaps and 40 fixes, the chat log matches its recorded count with no gap, and the fare line reconciles. All artifacts carry weight 1.0, so confidence is not discounted. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is engaged (no cross-party dispute history, no anti-farming pattern, no abuse counter, no sole impaired evidence, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor). No clause produces a referral on these facts — in particular POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire because there was no false arrival marker."},"discarded_claims":[]}

